Almost two years after nearly ascending a Valkyrie, I decided to try
something a bit different - ascending a Tourist.
Unfortunately, I couldn't play on alt.org due to a horrid college
internet connection, so I couldn't copy-paste all the text. This
screenshot will have to do: http://yfrog.com/17yafapp

I wound up using fourteen wishes and genociding a bunch of species
(including all liches, mind flayers, and ;) to ensure victory. In
fact, I was insanely lucky with wishes from the beginning. I wound up
finding a magic lamp before I even hit Minetown, then found three more
in Minetown itself (two at Izchak's and one at the general store). The
wand of wishing at the castle was fully charged, and I used blessed
charging to get three more, plus wresting the final charge from the
wand. I found yet another magic lamp inside the mazes underneath the
castle, and two more from pudding farming (forgive me) much later
after clearing out Gehennom. Had a few more wishes from thrones (two)
along the way. Still had three magic lamps (two blessed, one uncursed)
on me at the end.

I did everything I possibly could to survive. Had a full set of +5
armor (GDSM, AoR, T-Shirt, GoP, HoT, Speed Boots) and a +7 Grayswandir/
Silver Saber combo. I wound up using one of my many wishes on
Magicbane, and wound up barely using it. I found Cleaver inside Orcus
Town, and Trollsbane/Frost Brand/Mjollnir/Dragonbane from sacrificing
the many puddings (200+) that I farmed in Minetown (which happened to
have a sink and a co-aligned altar). By the way, on the unlikely
chance that anyone from the DevTeam reads this post, you should put in
a ritual in the next version to turn three or more Bane weapons into
some sort of Omnibane.

The puddings I farmed out of necessity - I had reached the Vibrating
Square, marked it, and was about to go kill Rodney when I realized I
had no idea which scroll was gold detection. I wound up farming
puddings and never finding ANY gold detection scrolls, but was able to
figure out which one was which by going down my Discoveries list and
figuring out I had all but two scrolls identified - the other turned
out to be Punishment.

With my posessions in hand (plus a blessed horn of plenty, a blessed
unicorn horn, a blessed can of grease, the PYEC, and 15 bottles of
holy water) I killed Rodney and grabbed the book to preform the
invocation. Going back up Gehennom turned out to be a lot tougher than
I thought. Even though I had taken plenty of time to dig a clear path
between the staircases, I wound up getting the Mysterious Force at
LEAST twenty times, until I finally managed to escape to the Castle
and (relative) safety. The Elemental Planes were, surprisingly, not
all that bad with gold detection to find the portal - except for Fire,
and even then that was largely due to the hundreds of resist messages
generated by the elementals. I had Rodney appear around five times,
and killed him each time with a Wand of Death blast.

My last bit of luck came from finding the correct High Altar on my
first try - in fact, I THOUGHT I was going to the center altar and
didn't realize until it was too late. However, with -50 AC and the
best sword in the game, nothing could even touch me. A few Wand of
Death blasts cleared out most of the area and let me get my 2 bits
from the High Priest of the Lady before offering up the amulet.

I think what I've taken away from this is that Tourist is definitely
not a weak role - although it turned out to be a pain trying to make
it to Minetown to do protection racket, even WITH the GDSM I was
wearing at the time. I've also learned the value of having your pet
kill everything for you.

I'd like to thank everyone who helped me with my near-ascension two
years ago, and the people who wrote the spoilers that I wound up
referring to so often to refresh my memory. I'd also like to thank The
Shrewd Dude and the Pudding Rights Society. Go team @!




